<title>BRAZIL: Brazil judge upholds Comgas auction.</title>
<headline>Brazil judge upholds Comgas auction.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Brazilian judge has ruled against an injuction that sought to block the sale of a minority stake in Sao Paulo state-owned gas firm Comgas, the Sao Paulo bourse said in a statement.</p>
<p>Last week, Sao Paulo's city government auctioned off its 19.86 percent voting stake in Comgas, which was acquired by Shell Brasil SA, a unit of Royal Dutch Shell, for a minimum price of 74 million reais.</p>
<p>Brazilian investment bank Bozano, Simonsen tried to have the sale invalidated, arguing that the auctioneer failed to acknowledge Bozano's bid during the sale.</p>
<p>Comgas, which is expected to be fully privatized in October, is controlled by the Sao Paulo state government, which holds an 80 percent stake in the firm.</p>
<p>Comgas distributes 3 million cubic meters of gas daily but it has agreed with Petrobras to increase its daily purchases to 1.5 million cubic meters of gas by 1998 and another 4 million daily by 1999.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
